text:
Is this from Crawgol? Wonderful! Despite all the turmoil in the world, we can't turn our back on the silithid threat. It is important to have people like Crawgol studying our enemy closely and learning its secrets for the fight ahead!

&lt;Tauna opens the book and glances over the first page. Her face falls.&gt;

Oh. Well. I suppose it's something, at least.

Zo'rau is wearing the pin.

&lt;Xy'nell's shoulders loosen.&gt;

Thank you, &lt;name&gt;. Now you and I must be careful.

The craftsmanship is good, but the quality is feeble at best.

&lt;Barm snaps the gauntlets in half and throws them to floor&gt;

You have proven yourself worthy of my tutelage however.

You got every single spider, right?

Either way, I'll just check that one off the list. No need to check up on your work.

&lt;Darius makes a squinched-up face.&gt;

&lt;The troll looks into the package.&gt;

You have my thanks.

I have been waiting for you to approach me, &lt;race&gt;.  I have identified you as the most promising &lt;race&gt; here in this strange town.  I have a task for you, if you would be willing to take it.

If the old draenei said to destroy the book, why didn't you?

&lt;Ramdor glares at you.&gt;

Bah, what's the difference. You might be greedy but at least you're honest.

Me on the other hand... I lied to get this book. I have no idea where these poor lost souls kept their treasure nor would I tell you if I did - however - I do have something for you. You did a good thing on this day. Perhaps a great thing... You should be rewarded.

By the way, welcome to the fold.

&lt;Ramdor points to the spirits.&gt;

I see... yes, I can work with this.

&lt;Kasim looks at the night elf's head.&gt;

Loramus Thalipedes, demon hunter.  I look forward to our reunion.

&lt;Solog Roark scans the horizon.&gt;

This will do. It's a good deepwater harbor. We can gut that old warship down there to make your first transport. Moving supplies up and down these cliffs will be a chore, but they'll give us additional security in case we're attacked.

We'll make it work. Are you ready to get building?

&lt;The raptor snatches the paperwork in her prehensile claws and holds the schematics up to her face, clucking her pointed teeth dismissively.&gt;

These are like the scrawling of children. Common sense precludes the routing of control hydraulics so near to the secondary stage burners! Still, this is salvageable.

Do you know how to refactor fuel matrixes for pressure variations at a fixed acceleration? No? Very well, perhaps you can do something else for me while I reconfigure the rocket...

&lt;Tiffany takes the bag from you and pulls out the jewels. She carefully looks over each one.&gt;

Good, they're all here. And from the looks of it, they're all the original jewels.

How did you deal with... actually, nevermind. I really don't care.

&lt;Timothy thumbs through the pages.&gt;

What a rare find, &lt;name&gt;. Excellent work on finding this.

As promised, here's a new design I've been holding on to.

&lt;Fleep wipes her face, plastering an enormous grease smear across her cheek.&gt;

What? The Captain said WHAT?

&lt;She shakes her pipe wrench threateningly.&gt;

It's HIS fault this big beast of an engine is delayed.

You're not Snivel. He was supposed to be here an hour ago! What have you done with him?

&lt;Roka seems to calm down when you tell her that you're looking for Snivel, too. Then, tears start to well up in her eyes.&gt;

This isn't like my sweet Snivel. Do you think something's happened to him?

Collect 25 Bird Feathers in your neighborhood.
25Bird Feathers (25)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(270210, 0, 25, null, null));

You did it! You found out what the Twilight's Hammer were up to and you stopped them dead in their tracks!

&lt;Mowi gets up on her tippy toes and gives you a kiss on the cheek.&gt;

Now I'm certain that I have something around here for you.

&lt;She begins rummaging around for your reward.&gt;

&lt;Rexxar nods.&gt;

You're here. Our strongest warriors are eager to attack the estate.

Let's not keep them waiting.

Ordinn sent you with these?

&lt;The smith examines the ingots.&gt;

He was right. Most of the magic is gone, but I can still sense traces of it. With some work and a few 'exotic' resources, I can forge you a powerful anti-demon sword from this metal.

Collect 5 Windrunner Memorabilia.
5Partially-Used Memento (5)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(249542, 0, 5, null, null));

And now we shall see what the future holds for you.

&lt;The Bone Witch casts the bones upon the rug in front of her.&gt;

Choose your fate, &lt;class&gt;.

&lt;Beads of sweat roll down Boog's overly large forehead as he reads the translated letter.&gt;

This is bad. Really, really bad. You have to warn Lord Fallowmere at Windshear Hold.

What in the... It's MOVING! The goblin balloon is taking off! We're too late!

&lt;Kilrok pages through the plans you discovered.&gt;

This explains much, &lt;name&gt;. No wonder our foes are so hellbent on taking the southern Barrens. It's at the center of their plans for the continent!

But they didn't account for us, did they &lt;class&gt;?

Collect 12 Spiteful Shadowgraft from wild creatures in the Bastion of Might.
12Spiteful Shadowgraft (12)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(247422, 0, 12, null, null));

&lt;That looks like the last of Art's rods.

You manage to salvage some of Art's bait with your catch. 

Waste not, want not&gt;

&lt;Saurfang grins.&gt;

It looks familiar... The Might of Kalimdor trampled a thousand bugs like this one in the desert of Silithus.

This is a different place - a different environment - but the result will be the same.

&lt;Saurfang looks you over.&gt;

You will bring pride and honor to the Horde in Northrend, &lt;name&gt;.

Ah, well done, friend. These are finer than I thought they'd be. They'll make a fine cloak.

&lt;Bertelm glances toward the inn.&gt;

Yes, a fine cloak it shall be.

Collect Golden Sunleaf at Stillwhisper Pond.
6Golden Sunleaf (6)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(245531, 0, 6, null, null));

Purchase a case of Bloodthistle Brandy, Mana Burner, and Sun-Kissed Tranquilla from vendors in Tranquillien.
Bloodthistle Brandy (1)
Mana Burner (1)
Sun-Kissed Tranquilla (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(249555, 0, 1, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon2').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(249556, 0, 1, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon3').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(249557, 0, 1, null, null));

&lt;Brann takes the fragments and begins reassembling them.&gt;

Well, ye definitely found more o' the Titan Disc, but ye found something else too.

Here, take a look at that!

Shiver me timbers and timber me shivers!  Ye found me beautiful eye!  Let's see if she still fits.

&lt;Kshhh-thunk&gt;

&lt;name&gt; ho!  Blimey, I can see!!

What in the world have you brought me?! Nat told you to ask me to turn THIS into a pole?

&lt;Marcia takes the severed lure from you. As she holds it close to the pearl, it begins to resonate with it.&gt;

That's interesting. There seems to be a connection between this and the pearl. Maybe turning this into a fishing rod can yield some interesting results...

Collect 6 Whole Uncursed Livers in the Serpent's Tail.
6Whole Uncursed Liver (6)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(278094, 0, 6, null, null));

&lt;Halford says a prayer for the deceased.&gt;

You do the Light's work, &lt;name&gt;.

I fear that our work has only just begun.

&lt;You recount your findings about the shrine in Drustvar to Samuel.&gt;

How fortunate for us that the inhabitants of that area used the same rocks to create their constructs from.

I suppose luck is on our side in the quest for these shrines.

&lt;Onatay looks over the fresh hides, nodding her head slowly.&gt;

Yes &lt;name&gt;, I can work with these. You work fast!

These hides will help us hold out for reinforcements longer. Thank you.

&lt;Stefan sifts through the foul components.&gt;

Well, it's far from perfect, but it'll have to do.

Now brace yourself, &lt;class&gt;. This is where it gets good....

&lt;The F.C.D. crackles with static.&gt;

Dreadwatch is lost? This is bad, &lt;name&gt;. Real bad.

If Dreadwatch is compromised it means we've lost Gilneas City.

Kota has asked for gorm gris?

&lt;Master Sha'lor beams with excitement.&gt;

I would be happy to oblige her request! Come, let me show you how this works.

Some very angry judges recently passed through here.

&lt;Archivist Fane grins.&gt;

Tell me everything you did to antagonize them. Don't skip a single detail!

&lt;Your trainer looks over the pistil and stamen, clearly impressed.&gt;

The Earthmother must have been feeling generous when she created the aethril.

Continue to focus on this part of the flower, &lt;name&gt;.

Is that?

&lt;Jane takes the locket and opens it tenderly. Tears begin to well up in her eyes as she closes it and tucks it away in her jacket.&gt;

Thank you.

&lt;Narkrall clenches the insignias in his weathered hand.&gt;

So, &lt;class&gt;. There's more to you than meets the eye.

Maybe your Horde can stand with the best of my warriors. Let's try you out...

Your work is appreciated, soldier.

&lt;The commander leans in close, and whispers:&gt;

&lt;race&gt;... if you're still interested, I have one more small task for you...

Is that what I think it is?

&lt;Ta'xera examines the stonefiend closely.&gt;

In perfect condition! I can't wait to study every intricacy.

Hunt down beasts around Har'athir and collect materials to forge a Ka'dani weapon.
Chloroceros Bone (1)
4Grovecrawler Fang (4)
4Lasher Vine (4)
4Sporeglider's Tail Spore (4)
 Ketan found during the hunt (2)
 Lashers (1)
 Chloroceros (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(255259, 0, 1, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon2').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(255258, 0, 4, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon3').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(255260, 0, 4, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon4').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(255261, 0, 4, null, null));

Collect 6 Sweetsaw Blooms around the Ring of Glory.
6Sweetsaw Bloom (6)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(262886, 0, 6, null, null));

She wanted this?

&lt;Kane cracks open the jar slightly. His eyes begin to water immediately.&gt;

T-thanks.

&lt;Coughing, Kane hastily re-seals the jar.&gt;

That must have cost a lot. Let me pay you back with a tip.

A new species!  Are you sure?

&lt;Lauranna flips through pages of notes and diagrams.&gt;

Nice job, &lt;name&gt;.  We'll have to add this one to our list.  How does "Purple Leafed Aelarathrium" sound to you?  It does have a ring to it.

Orcs?! They were sunk and stranded too?  And now the Alliance are on the island? Do you think they're going to kill us?

&lt;Sassy looks thoughtful.&gt;

I think it's time for a little sitdown with these orcs.

Collect 100 Sparks of War in Voidstorm, while in War Mode.
100Spark of War (100)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(219934, 0, 100, null, null));

You did it! Excellent work, my boy. You found out what the Twilight's Hammer were up to and you stopped them dead in their tracks!

&lt;Examiner Rowe pats you on the back with his bony hand.&gt;

Now I'm certain that I have something around here for you.

&lt;He begins rummaging around for your reward.&gt;

&lt;The duke looks at you a moment and nods.&gt;

You're inflicting horrible mental trauma on the Jotunheim vrykul. This is where they were first reawakened. It is a place of significant importance to them, second only to Ymirheim.

You must keep up the pressure there while I hold the vault from the assault of the Lich King.

&lt;Karnum opens and reads Korrah's Report.&gt;

This is alarming news, indeeed, &lt;race&gt; - something we have no shortage of here.

I shall call a council regarding the issue. You will be summoned if you are needed.

&lt;Weldon holds Alexi's head up to his face and begins speaking.&gt;

You no-good, backstabbing son-of-a-goat! Your greed is only surpassed by my own!

As for you my peasant friend, you have served me well. Here are your just rewards!

Recover Logistical Intel from the ethereals at the Eastern Manaforge.
12Infantry's Data-Node (12)
Nullframe Holoprint (1)
Soul Lattice Holoprint (1)
Glittering Crypt Holoprint (1)
 Holoprints Collected (3)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(274990, 0, 12, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon2').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(275477, 0, 1, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon3').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(275687, 0, 1, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon4').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(275689, 0, 1, null, null));

Ay, mon. I been expectin' you.

&lt;To'bor points west.&gt;

Take a peek. Across dat tundra be death, mon... death.

Collect 6 pieces of Twilight Weaponry from cultists at the Sanctum of the Moon.
6Twilight Weaponry (6)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(249528, 0, 6, null, null));

Y'got these fer me, laddie? I... I don't know what ta say!

Here, take this. It's the least I can do.

&lt;Hemet buries his nose deep into the bear hide.&gt;

&lt;Jani sniffs the air, smelling your wet garbage.&gt;

Ya brought ol' Jani a present! What ya got there? Let me see it.

&lt;Jani begins rooting through the pile of trash you have brought.&gt;

Oh, yes, and some of this, mmm, mmmhm, yes, oh that's sticky...

&lt;Jani seems pleased with your offering, and is paying no attention to you any longer.&gt;

&lt;Ewan shakes his head as he accepts the pack from you&gt;

I don't think Flanis realized how heavily guarded the Deathforge would be. Now that we know what's really going on there, I don't blame them. I just wish Flanis had known that when he went in.

I can only hope there's something here that will help us shut down the Deathforge once and for all.

&lt;A plaque reads:

Who you meet on your journey, makes the trip worth taking.

Gorm was a good fighter.&gt;

&lt;Apprentice Tanmar takes the three Singing Fragments and looks at them dubiously.&gt;

You can tell there is power here. I... hope I can fuse them safely. Here goes nothing. Or everything. Heh.

&lt;Apprentice Tanmar takes out a vial of viscous, golden liquid and begins piecing them together. The liquid flashes with light, and the citrine is whole again. He hands you the repaired citrine.&gt;

Impressed? Don't be. It was fancy glue, to be honest. But hopefully this ring'll further our knowledge of the isle!

Tillik! Dear friend I'm so glad you have returned! All of the acolytes missed your witty banter after the evening chants.

&lt;Iktis looks back towards you.&gt;

Yes, now your great test is done. You have fulfilled the requirements of The Parchment of Dust!

I see you brought back a gift from Highmountain.

&lt;Nalthanis thumbs through the pages.&gt;

This is fascinating! Look here, &lt;name&gt;, some formulas for cloak enchantments. I believe these would come in handy for us at this point in time.

&lt;General Twinbraid hurls his axeblade into the dirt, his voice quiet but his body quivering with disbelief and rage.&gt;

That was my boy, &lt;name&gt;. My only boy.

They've made it personal, &lt;class&gt;. Personal.

&lt;Earthmender Torlok takes the Cipher of Damnation from you.&gt;

You have done as the elements asked. For that, we are grateful. While you will be rewarded, trouble still looms. The spirits of fire are in turmoil. A claim has been made. the Cipher of Damnation is known by another.

It is cryptic, I know, but that is all that the spirits would have me know. That and this symbol...

&lt;Earthmender Torlok turns around and points to the sky.&gt;

What could it mean?

I heard your people had washed up on our shores, but I did not expect to find one washed up on my very doorstep! What brings you here, stranger?

&lt;You explain about your search for Prince Anduin, and describe the boy to the pandaren.&gt;

Very interesting! And so the Pearlfin sent you to me, did they?

&lt;Reshad gazes into the inky orb.&gt;

Amazing. To think Terokk used this very orb to commune with Anzu. One could become quite the darkweaver with an implement such as this.

Come, let's get it safely to the Veil.

Collect 36 Pungent Leech Legs in the Serpent's Tail.
36Pungent Leech Leg (36)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(277935, 0, 36, null, null));

I wasn't sure how those refiners would hold up under stress. I'm glad you fixed 'em!

&lt;Jazz casually flips a small kaja'mite crystal between his fingers.&gt;

Do you think I could patent and license the schematics? The royalties could keep me outta the field if I charge enough.

They knew all of that? And who the hell is this Grand Admiral Westwind that he spoke of?!

&lt;The high executor grumbles to himself about hating surprises.&gt;

Better that we know than have to guess. I hope that you left your... er, my mark.

Deliver Hieron's journal to Riftblade Astre at Locus Point.
Hieron's Journal (1)
A Worn Envelope (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(248207, 0, 1, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon2').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(248209, 0, 1, null, null));

Please do not wash yourself in the sacred waters of the Throne.

&lt;Elementalist Lo'ap holds a prepared caracoli tablet up.&gt;

You place this under your tongue and allow it ample time to dissolve. Once it has dissolved, you will be able to breathe water as if it were air.

You have word from the spy mistress?

&lt;The agent looks around to make sure that no one is watching as she puts down her shovel.&gt;

Let me see those plans.

You've done well, young one. I recall a gnome not too long ago completing that trial as well.

Her story was quite the read. But between you and me, gnomes smell like porridge.

&lt;Kronah looks off into the distance, lost in thought for a moment.&gt;

But you are now a bearer of the Bloodshed Contract and one step closer to your final prize.

&lt;Kronah quirks a grin at you and goes back about her business.&gt;

&lt;Pang surveys the area around his farm.&gt;

Well, they're not ALL gone yet, but there's less of them. And they aren't holding their ears quite as high anymore.

I'd guess that they're scared of you, &lt;name&gt;.

You got the hair?!

&lt;Ms. Xiulan laughs audibly.&gt;

Oh, I wish I could have been there to see the look on his face. Nevertheless, a deal's a deal.

&lt;The Far Seer makes sure to hold the item by the string, carefully avoiding the dead ogre's fist.&gt;

Strange indeed.  I will pass this on to my contacts in the east, near the Mosh'Ogg's main camp.  I have a feeling that they'll be interested in these strange scars.

You have my thanks, &lt;race&gt;.

&lt;Nazgrim listens as you recount the day's events.&gt;

We take the bell... and the Alliance takes Dalaran. That escalated quickly.

War is coming, &lt;name&gt;. Be on your toes.

&lt;Brann looks at the disk as you hold it up.&gt;

I can't tell if there's anything stored there or not! You have to tell me what happened.

&lt;You describe the data retrieval process.&gt;

So it worked? At least we can count on Mimir to be systematic. Can't say that for the rest of these Keepers from what I've been hearing...

You seek training?

&lt;The pandaren studies your physique for several seconds, without speaking.&gt;

Alright.

And you returned victorious, just as I thought! I told Saurfang you'd be fine.

&lt;Hellscream grunts knowingly.&gt;

Perhaps this will show that old dog that he doesn't have all the answers, eh?

&lt;Kalecgos listens to your account of recent events.&gt;

It was wise of Tarecgosa to send you to me, &lt;class&gt;.

Though your vision in the Nexus was almost certainly an elaborate illusion, it would be irresponsible of me not to investigate it.

Now look at that...

&lt;The Rokk takes a sip of the concoction and his face twists into a bizarre mask of pain and delight.&gt;

Sweet A'dal that's good!  A cook with your potential shouldn't be without his proper materials.  Take some of my extra stock and make me proud.

Return triumphant! Valor stick to you like reek of old grease.

&lt;Walkmay pauses, sniffing gingerly.&gt;

That a lot of valor!

&lt;Parvink is covered in bleeding scratches and shredded leaves.&gt;

Hey, not bad! We'll call it a tie. This jungle don't scare me for nothin'.

Maybe we can hunt some more tomorrow?

&lt;Anduin looks like a crumpled doll. He lays as still as a stone, and the only movement comes from the frigid air ruffling his fair, golden hair.&gt;

&lt;You sit quietly for a while, until the cold settles into your bones. The bell is destroyed, but the silence is deafening.&gt;

&lt;Out of the corner of your eye, you see the slightest flicker from the boy's hand. You lean in close. He breathes - but just barely! Anduin is alive!&gt;

That... wasn't what I expected to find out. 

&lt;Lilian clears her throat.&gt;

Family drama aside, whatever the old queen used to be, she'll be a big problem for us when she inevitably shows up on the battlefield.

Brilliant work!

&lt;Tulra tucks the pearls away beneath her armor.&gt;

Now I just need you and Legionnaire Nazgrim to get me safely out of here.  I can handle the studies from there on.

You have done it!

&lt;Goraluk takes the items from your hands, and turns his back for a few moments&gt;

Now, I will touch this Sigil to your hand, and the entrance to the Crucible will open at your touch. Good luck.

Return the tainted sample to Lady Darkglen.
Tainted Sample (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(270562, 0, 1, null, null));

&lt;You report your findings to Erunak, who listens distractedly while flipping through the journal you located.&gt;

So... the naga have conscripted sea giants to their cause? This is disturbing.

Adelee's journal confirms my fears. The naga have infiltrated the Abyssal Maw once again, and this time they have a powerful weapon with them: Sharas'dal. Our task is clear.

&lt;Nourman carefully inspects the fangs.&gt;

Checks out. Strange that you got so many. 

Say, you don't look like a venthyr. 

&lt;Nourman shrugs.&gt;

Don't matter to me. You got the fangs, you go inside. Them's the rules.

&lt;Lady Sylvanas Windrunner grimaces in pain.&gt;

This... is not over. Godfrey and his traitorous allies will pay for what they have done as will the remaining Alliance forces occupying Lordaeron.

Our work has only just begun.

We've already lost many brave warriors to this cursed wasteland. I have little interest in sending more untested recruits to the slaughter.

&lt;Nazgrel glares at you sternly through his ragged wolf-mask&gt;

Still, if General Krakork sent you to me, he must have seen something in you. What say you then, &lt;name&gt;? Will you serve your warchief with honor?

Collect 10 Void-Infused Morsels and 6 Glaring Glowcaps outside of the Howling Ridge.
10Void-Infused Morsel (10)
6Glaring Glowcap (6)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(246372, 0, 10, null, null));
WH.ge('icon-list-icon2').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(246661, 0, 6, null, null));

Whew, that was close. This whole thing has really taught me to value the beauty of nature.

&lt;The goblin breaks into laughter.&gt;

Really had you going there, huh? Still, think I'll leave Abyssal Excavation alone for awhile.

&lt;The King is studying maps of Tanaan Jungle and the surrounding area.&gt;

&lt;name&gt;! The Alliance owes you a great debt for establishing this garrison. Thanks to your bravery and commanding leadership, we've fought this war here on Draenor, instead of amongst our own homes and farmsteads.

It's time now to finish this. Are you ready for the final campaign?

Recover 30 Forgotten Memorial Tributes.
30Forgotten Memorial Tribute (30)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(276255, 0, 30, null, null));

&lt;You recount your findings about the Vol'dun shrine to Seshuli&gt;

Dat desert is a fools home if ya ask me. Good thing de shrine still stands dere and you were able to fix it.

I'm still reading de journal trying to gather more information for you.

I knew they weren't here to see the sights.

&lt;The sergeant examines the plans you captured, his eyes wide.&gt;

This is more serious than we thought! This is no mere raid. The Dark Irons intend to cripple the defense of Ironforge itself!

&lt;The High Commander reads the missive and then crumples it up.&gt;

Do you know where the people on this list are now? Take a look outside, near the front gate. They're the ones hanging from the arches.

Ghoul bait...

&lt;Aggra gives you the eye as if she doesn't quite believe what you are telling her.&gt;

I am not easily impressed, but if what you are telling me is true, then I have never before heard of such a thing.

You have my thanks, &lt;name&gt;.

Heard Westfall was in some deep doody.

&lt;Parker doesn't even turn to face you.&gt;

Well, we got our own set of problems here. See them gnolls out there? Looks like they're actin' up again. I don't like it. Don't like it one bit.

Mahka sent you?

&lt;Mankrik's fury quells for a moment.&gt;

It is a small comfort. But nothing can console me until I am done here.

&lt;The small snapdragon voraciously tears into the morsel. It seems to be energized by both the meat and the caffeinated Kaja'Cola the meat was soaked in.

It looks up at you with gratitude in its eyes. 

It will remember you.&gt;

Collect 7 Vibrant Crownfeathers in the Serpent's Tail.
7Vibrant Crownfeather (7)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(277920, 0, 7, null, null));

The Greeter will soon answer all of your questions. That is its purpose, after all.

&lt;Kleia smiles at you.&gt;

I hope you are excited. I certainly am!

Hmm... How am I going to package this?

I have an idea!

&lt;Beezil writes Youngroot on a label and slaps it onto a bottle of adder oil.&gt;

&lt; He throws the Youngroot in the bushes behind him.&gt;

Perfect!

Haha!

&lt;Geraldine spits again out of her tooth gap.&gt;

Had it comin' they did!

COWARD!!! Vanessa VanCleef is a dirty human coward! How dare she flee from battle against the Horde and leave her unworthy subordinate to fight!

&lt;Kagtha composes herself.&gt;

No matter. Her ship is reward enough. The citizens of Stormwind will bear first hand witness to our awe inspiring power using a ship made in part by the very architect of their city!

What's this then? Another novice come to learn the ways of blood-scribing?

Very well, for which contract do you need a quill?

&lt;You explain to Miju that you've learned all four contracts and need a quill to invoke all of them.&gt;

ALL FOUR?! Oh my, it's been... let's see here...

