&lt;Solog Roark takes in the view of his harbor one final time.&gt;

We built it all for nothing, &lt;class&gt;. Gul'dan will claim whatever your troops do not destroy.

Next time, I will build something that will last.

&lt;Angorla holds the glowing citrine in her hand before holding it out to you.&gt;

That seemed to do the trick... I've never felt such energy radiate from such a small crystal before. 

The runes engraved on it are quite ancient and very powerful.

Another plant, fallen...

&lt;The druid attempts to blink back tears, and fails.&gt;

DAMN YOU, NIGHTMARE! DAMN YOUUUUU!!!

&lt;Aska examines the ingredients you have chosen.&gt;

Mmmhmmm. Yes. Well done!

I could not have chosen better myself.

&lt;The arakkoa merchant looks you up and down.&gt;

Well-equipped, aren't we? Azik is betting you are someone of importance to your people.

Come closer, friend. Speak with me for just a moment.

&lt;Rana begins speaking in a whisper and places the bone fragment in a small pouch of a necklace she is wearing.&gt;

Dis means a lot to me. 

While I will never be a king, I will have de Loa of Kings watching over me for de rest of my days.

&lt;Rana dusts off her hands as she returns to her normal volume.&gt;

If I recall correctly, I promised to teach you everything  I know about gathering bones, yes?

&lt;Rana begins explaining which bones can be easily removed from the socket without breaking the bones.&gt;

&lt;Lou puts his hands to his ears and starts talking loudly.&gt;

STOP! STOP! STOP! I don't wanna hear it! I don't wanna know and I don't care! That kind of information is liable to get you killed 'round these parts.

I got one more bit of information for you and then we're done!

&lt;Stonehead scratches his head and peers at the document.&gt;

Me see lots of wax blobs.

&lt;Stonehead thinks very hard, moving his lips as he tries to sound out words.&gt;

Umm... maybe... it... say... Me go party with best bud?

Yay! Me go party with best bud!

You did it! You did it!

&lt;Jinky grabs you and gives you a big smooch on the cheek! She then regains her dignity and smooths her clothes.&gt;

Thanks for saving my Speedbarge, Captain &lt;name&gt;.

Your work is appreciated, soldier.

&lt;The warlord leans in close, and whispers:&gt;

&lt;race&gt;... if you're still interested, I have one more small task for you...

There they are! Back into the sty with you three, now!

&lt;Liang looks up at you.&gt;

Thank you, neighbor. I'm truly grateful for your assistance.

You came upon me in a moment of reflection.

&lt;Velen peers at you with a tired expression.&gt;

There is no time for such sentiment. We must press on.

&lt;Bargus looks up from his anvil.&gt;

Another new arrival. 

Here to lend a hand to our efforts?

&lt;Mordant produces a small sheet of paper and a pen, beginning to scribble down notes on your findings.&gt;

From your findings, the spirits in this place must amount to everyone who ever lived on this land, not just the previous occupants.

Something has been corrupting and killing them. Those who follow don't learn the truth until it's too late. We have to put an end to this, &lt;name&gt;!

&lt;The chief listens as you describe the seer's vision.&gt;

Well, I don't know about any of that, but we could certainly use your help around here. Behold the rocket behind me! That's the X-52...

Isn't it the most beautiful thing you've ever seen?

