&lt;Sylvanas nods at you.&gt;

I will prepare our forces and have them at the ready.

&lt;You explain to Surkhan what has happened up to this point.&gt;

It would seem that Jin'do has survived, and he is rallying his brothers to once again summon Hakkar into this world.  It was good of you to come to speak with me.

There is not much we can do now but to wait, and watch.  Jin'do is weak, and prime for striking, but I must wait for word from Rastakhan before issuing orders.  Until then, you and your raptor will have to wait.

&lt;The archmage is out of breath.&gt;

Give me - give me a moment. Pshew.

&lt;name&gt;, that was incredible! You are possibly the greatest &lt;class&gt; I've ever had the honor to fight alongside.

&lt;Archmage Vargoth's image examines you as you convey Ravandwyr's message.&gt;

Ravandwyr has everything a master can expect of his apprentice. When I gave him the staff and told him to flee, I hoped that he would use it to find help and free me once Kael'thas's forces withdrew from the tower. Since then, I have learned a great deal about the nature of the curse.

It can be broken, &lt;name&gt;, but it will require your help.

Have you done that before? Your skill with my machete seemed practiced.

&lt;The brave looks at you warily.&gt;

I'll take it back from you now, &lt;class&gt;.

&lt;Brother Nimetz opens up a pouch and lets you place the crystal inside.&gt;

I knew they'd have some more of this substance.  I'm going to send this to my contacts at Fort Livingston, to the south.  Hopefully they'll have some more luck with it.

Thank you for everything, &lt;name&gt;.

