&lt;Lieutenant Fairweather grins at the story that you tell her about your adventures at Boulder'mok.&gt;

Ah, I wish that I could have been there with you.  Let me tell you something, &lt;name&gt;: never accept any duty that keeps you from the glory of the battlefield!

Hah!  After all of the ogre killing that you've done, are there any still left in these mountains for me?!

&lt;The murloc spirit looks upon you sadly.&gt;

