&lt;Nork scoffs.&gt;

Prisoners? These aren't prisoners. They're cowardly dogs! Just look at 'em. Did you know that without exception, every single one of these yellow-bellied "soldiers" came to our gates and surrendered their arms and armor?

From what we've been able to gather, these men and women are discharged and sent back to their homes if captured by us.

&lt;Nork spits.&gt;

Pathetic...

&lt;The smith frowns and examines the ingots.&gt;

I'll be frank with you, &lt;class&gt;. I'm a relic of an age when cooperation with the Horde was unthinkable.

I am not so blind as to see that we do not have common enemies. I will help you to reforge the anti-demon weapon but it's going to take a lot of hard work and a few 'exotic' resources.

&lt;You tell Harbinger Mikolaas of the survey team's fate. He accepts the crystal from you, but remains silent for a long moment.&gt;

They were good men, &lt;name&gt;, and they knew their mission would be dangerous. I'm grateful for your help in locating the team and recovering the crystal.



We've lost too many good men already, and our mission has only just begun.

&lt;After hearing your retelling of Mevris' plan, Daniss nods thoughtfully.&gt;

I'm glad you were able to assist him. He has been gone for some time now. Hopefully with this creature now deceased, there is one less obstacle before he can come home.

And good work with the scales. These appear to be perfect for the task.

The Brashtide!?  I thought they were dead and gone YEARS ago!

&lt;Revilgaz listens intently as you relay the information you gathered.&gt;

No, that absolutely makes sense.  And it's not good news either.  The Brashtide are formidable foes, and if their numbers are anywhere near what they were before they disappeared, we're in for a nasty battle.

&lt;The paladin frowns.&gt;

That's quite a gruesome trophy collection you have there. I would have believed you if you had simply said they were dead. Regardless, thank you for having the foresight to take care of them.

The Twilight Gate will soon be ours. Time to move up to the Twilight Citadel.

